R"VG(
# news3.vg (H-04's second pass): the news's register, continued: the collapse as the papers saw it (the signs, the towns left, the
# people leaving), the sky, the feasts, the other people, the institutions, the discoveries, the faith, a deed, a regency, and the quiet
# week (`news.none`: what a paper prints when nothing happened, which is most weeks).

news.sign
  {news.h.sign}\n{news.sign.m} {news.sign.t}
news.h.sign
  Concern grows
  Questions asked
  A strange season
  (stage>=2) The trouble spreads
  (stage>=2) What is happening?
news.sign.m
  It is reported that {$e.sign}.
  Readers have written to say that {$e.sign}.
  Our correspondent writes that {$e.sign}, and that nobody in the town will talk about it.
  It is now confirmed that {$e.sign}; the rumours of last {season.any} were, if anything, too mild.
  (stage>=2) Again: {$e.sign}.
news.sign.t
  {news.said} that there is no cause for alarm.
  This paper has asked the council for an explanation and received none.
  {news.said} that a commission will look into it, and report by {season.next}.
  The old people say they have seen it before; the young ones say the old people say that about everything.
  (stage>=1) Families are asking the paper whether they should leave. The paper does not know.
  (stage>=1) The price of a cart has doubled in a month, and of a {vessel.one.n} of {crop} more.
  The priests of {holyplace} have called for {news.rite.imp.x}.
  The {herd} have been restless, the farmers say, and the {bird} are gone from the roofs.
news.rite.imp.x
  a fast
  a day of silence
  prayers at every hearth
  the old rites to be kept again

news.abandoned
  {news.h.left}\n{news.left.m} {news.left.t}
news.h.left
  {$e.place} abandoned
  The last of {$e.place}
  {$e.place} empty
news.left.m
  The last residents of {$e.place} have left. The town has been empty for some months.
  ($e.left=river) {$e.place} is given up: the river has moved away from it, and the wharves stand over dry mud.
  ($e.left=wells) {$e.place} is given up, its water gone; the last carts left with the last barrels.
  ($e.left=mine) The mine at {$e.place} is worked out, and the town with it.
  ($e.left=soil) The fields round {$e.place} will grow nothing more, and its people have gone to where something grows.
  ($e.left=cities) Nobody young is left in {$e.place}, and now nobody old either.
  ($e.left=taken) {$e.place} has been given up to the enemy without a fight.
  ($e.left=collapse|$e.left=cause) {$e.place} has emptied, family by family, until there was nobody left to post the notice.
news.left.t
  Its {houses} stand open to the weather.
  The council has taken the bells away for safe keeping.
  (has:$e.place.landmark) Of the town, only {$e.place.landmark} still looks as it did.
  A watchman will stay until {season.next}, the council says, and then he will not.
  Its people are said to be at {$home} and in the coast towns, and its {herd} on the roads.
  The {crop} fields about the town are going back to grass and {tree}.

news.exodus
  {news.h.exo}\n{news.exo.m} {news.exo.t}
news.h.exo
  Mass departures
  They are leaving
  The roads are full
news.exo.m
  {#$e.value:about} people are reported to have left {$e.place} in the last month.
  ($e.whither=sea) {#$e.value:about} have taken ship from {$e.place}, and the boats come back empty for more.
  ($e.whither=mountains) {#$e.value:about} have left {$e.place} for the mountains with what they could carry.
  ($e.whither=south|$e.whither=north) {#$e.value:about} have left {$e.place} for the {$e.whither}, where they have heard it is better.
  ($e.whither=sky) The ships have taken {#$e.value:about} from {$e.place}; the launch was watched by everyone who stayed.
news.exo.t
  The carters are charging what they like.
  The {herd} of the leavers are being sold at {town.open} for almost nothing.
  The houses they left have their doors open and their lamps on the tables.
  {news.said} that they will come back when things are better.
  They take {vessel} of {crop} and the {colour.holy} cloth from {holyplace}, and little else.

# ---- the sky -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.omen
  ($e.omen=comet) The comet returns\nThe comet has returned, as the astronomers predicted; it was last seen in our grandparents' time. {news.omen.t}
  ($e.omen=eclipse) Eclipse\nThe sun was eclipsed at noon yesterday, and {news.eclipse.m}. {news.omen.t}
  ($e.omen=aurora) Lights in the north\nThe lights were in the north sky over {$e.place} for three nights running. {news.omen.t}
  ($e.omen=falling) A falling star\nA fireball crossed the sky over {$e.place} at night, and some say they heard it. {news.omen.t}
  ($e.omen=newstar) A new star\nA star nobody has seen before is shining {news.newstar.m}. {news.omen.t}
  ($e.omen=redmoon) The red moon\n{moon} rose red over {$e.place}, as red as anyone can remember. {news.omen.t}
news.eclipse.m
  the {bird} went to roost at midday
  the {herd} lay down in the fields
  crowds watched it through smoked glass in {town.open}
  the bells rang by order of the council, to the confusion of the {herd}
news.newstar.m
  low in the evening sky
  near {star}, brighter every night
  where the old charts show nothing
news.omen.t
  It will be visible after dark for some weeks.
  The astronomers of {city} say it means nothing; the fortune-tellers of {$home} say otherwise.
  Children have been allowed to stay up to see it.
  {news.omen.bad}
news.omen.bad
  Some are saying it is a bad sign, as they always do.
  The old people of {$home} are counting it among the signs, as they count everything.

news.festival
  {$e.place} celebrates\n{$e.place} marked the {#$e.value:ord} year of its founding with {news.fest.how}. {news.fest.t}
news.fest.how
  a procession and fireworks
  {feast.custom} and speeches
  a dinner for the oldest families and a fair for everyone else
  a holiday, a parade and a great deal of {drink}
news.fest.t
  The {colour.holy} flags were out in every street.
  The oldest resident, who admits to ninety, cut the bread.
  Nobody went to work the next day either.
  The band played {news.tune} until the band could not.
  {feast.custom} lasted until morning, as it should.

# ---- the other people --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.contact
  Strangers at {$e.place}\nPeople who are not of the {people} have been met near {$e.place}. They call themselves the {other}. {news.contact.t}
news.contact.t
  They are said to be peaceful, and to have brought {news.contact.gift}.
  Nobody yet speaks their language, but they understand prices.
  {news.said} that envoys will be sent.
news.contact.gift
  salt
  cloth of a weave nobody here can make
  beasts we have no name for
  a great deal of curiosity
news.treaty
  Treaty with the {other}\nA treaty has been signed with the {other} at {$e.place}, {news.treaty.m}.
news.treaty.m
  and the frontier roads will be open from {season.next}
  and the traders of both peoples are pleased
  and nobody is quite sure what it says
news.otherend
  The {other}\nThere has been no word from the {other} for a year. Their towns are reported empty, and {news.otherend.t}.
news.otherend.t
  the traders who went to look came back quickly and would not say what they saw
  their fields are going back to grass
  nobody can say where they have gone

# ---- the institutions, the discoveries, the faith, a deed, a regency -----------------------------------------------------------
news.institution
  {$e.instname}\n{$e.instname} was founded yesterday {news.inst.t}.
news.inst.t
  , with speeches
  , to the surprise of nobody who had been asked for money
  (has:$e.a) by {$e.a:full}
  , and has already met twice
news.discovery
  A discovery\n{news.disc.m} {news.disc.t}
news.disc.m
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} has returned from an expedition with remarkable news.
  ($e.discovery=farshore has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} has come back from over the sea with word of a coast nobody had seen.
  ($e.discovery=source has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} has followed {river} to its source, and found it smaller than the river deserves.
  ($e.discovery=pass has:$e.a) {$e.a:name} has found a way over {mountain} that a cart can take.
  ($e.discovery=round) The learned now agree that the world is round, which the sailors say they knew.
  The expedition sent from {$e.place} has come home with [maps|specimens|stories|less than it took].
news.disc.t
  A lecture on it will be given at the hall, with lantern pictures.
  The council has voted the explorers a dinner of {food} and {drink}.
  Not everyone believes it, least of all the {craft} guild, which was not consulted.
news.faith
  ($e.faith=schism) A split in the faith\nThe faithful of {$e.place} are divided, and two services are held where there was one.
  ($e.faith=reformed has:$e.a) The rites reformed\n{$e.a:full} has changed the old rites at {$e.place}, and everyone has an opinion.
  ($e.faith=reformed !has:$e.a) The rites reformed\nThe old rites have been changed at {$e.place}, and everyone has an opinion.
  ($e.faith=preached has:$e.a) A new preacher\n{$e.a:full} is preaching at {$e.place}, and the hall cannot hold the crowds.
  ($e.faith=preached !has:$e.a) A new faith\nA new faith is being preached at {$e.place}, and the hall cannot hold the crowds.
  ($e.faith=closed) The temples closed\nThe temples have been closed by order, and their keepers sent home.
  ($e.faith=persecution) Arrests at {$e.place}\nThe faithful of {$e.place} are being arrested, it is said, for holding the old rites.
news.deed
  (has:$e.a) {$e.a:name}\n{news.deed.m}
news.deed.m
  ($e.deed=song) A song by {$e.a:name} is being sung in every street of {$e.place}, and some streets would like it to stop.
  ($e.deed=book|$e.deed=chronicle) A book by {$e.a:name} of {$e.place} is said to be in every house that has a shelf.
  ($e.deed=book|$e.deed=chronicle) {$e.a:name} of {$e.place} has written a book about {news.booksubject}, and the printers cannot print it fast enough.
  ($e.deed=map) The new map of the land made by {$e.a:name} shows {$e.place} smaller than {$e.place} thought.
  ($e.deed=healed) The doctor {$e.a:name} has stopped the fever at {$e.place}, and the town has given a dinner.
  ($e.deed=theory) {$e.a:name} has published a new account of the world, which the old accounts dispute.
  ($e.deed=taught) {$e.a:name} has taught at {$e.place} for many years, and the old pupils gave a dinner this week.
  ($e.deed=frieze|$e.deed=pictures|$e.deed=gardens) The new work of {$e.a:name} at {$e.place} can be seen on the rest day.
  ($e.deed=laws|$e.deed=hunt|$e.deed=sailed) {$e.a:full} is the talk of {$e.place} this week.
news.regency
  A regent\n{$e.a:full} will rule for {$e.b:name}, who is a child, until {$e.b:name} comes of age.

# ---- the quiet week ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
news.none
  {news.quiet.h}\n{news.quiet.b} {news.quiet.t}
news.quiet.h
  Nothing to report
  A quiet week
  From the provinces
  Around the towns
  The week
news.quiet.b
  It has been a quiet week across the land; the council sat twice and decided nothing.
  The {crop} is said to be average in the south and a little better in the north.
  The roads are open and the markets full, and prices are steady.
  The rest day passed without incident, the police report, apart from the usual.
  {festival} was kept in the towns, with {feast.custom} as always.
  From the hill towns, nothing but weather; from the coast, nothing but fish.
  The provinces report {weather.now}, a good price for {herd}, and a wedding in every second village.
news.quiet.t
  This paper is glad of it.
  We will report something when something happens.
  Readers with news are asked to bring it to the office, with a {vessel.one.n} of {fruit} if possible.
  The {bird} are back on the roofs, and that is the news.
  The {herd} are fat and the {crop} is green, and the paper has nothing to add.
news.booksubject
  the founding of {city}
  the {craft} trade and its secrets
  the year of the great {weather}
  a family of {$e.place}, very like the writer's
  the rivers, and the {fish} in them
)VG"
